<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Martin (island)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Martin is an island in the north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, divided by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-concordia">Treaty of Concordia</a> of 1648 between a French northern part and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> southern part, Sint Maarten. The French part was owned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> from 1651 to 1665, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a> and other islands. Today the French side is an overseas collectivity and the Dutch side a constituent country of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-martin-island.jpg" alt="Saint Martin (island)" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hogweard · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Martin_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
